---
import ContentLayout from "astro-theme-university/layouts/ContentLayout.astro";
import SessionsGrid from "../../components/SessionsGrid.astro";
import { sessionLabels, siteConfig } from "../../site-config";
---

<ContentLayout
  title={sessionLabels.plural}
  description="Twelve weeks, twelve methods, one day taken apart and rebuilt"
  {...siteConfig}
>
  <p>
    Each week is a lab. You arrive with a record of your own day and leave with
    a result about it — or, more often than you would like, with a reason the
    result cannot be trusted.
  </p>

  <p>
    The twelve weeks are not twelve topics. They are twelve <em>methods</em>,
    each introduced once and each depending on the ones before it, so the order
    is not a matter of taste: you cannot take something away and put it back
    before you have decided what you are measuring, and you cannot understand
    why your worst day improved until you have watched a whole class's worst
    days improve together.
  </p>

  <p>
    Four of the weeks ask you to change something about your sleep, your eating
    or your caffeine. Those four carry a stopping rule, a limit and an
    alternative protocol for anyone who should not take part — printed on the
    page, not in a handbook. The alternative is never a lesser version of the
    week. In one case it teaches the lesson better.
  </p>

  <SessionsGrid />
</ContentLayout>
